    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "What this dashboard is not",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 49
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "\n**It is not the invoice.** Prometheus holds counts over time with no account\nattached. Every number here is an instance-wide aggregate.\n\nFor money, in order of authority:\n\n1. **The credit ledger** in Postgres is the record of what each account was granted, bought and burned; **Stripe** holds the charges, refunds and disputes behind the purchases.\n2. **`usage_events` in Postgres** is what the invoice is built from. Nine event\n   types, written synchronously, never updated after insertion. The console\n   shows the per-account view under sandbox spend; `Fountain.Billing` has the\n   aggregates.\n3. **PostHog**, on the **Fountain / Finance** dashboard, holds the same nine\n   metering events per person, so \"which accounts drive the sandbox bill\" is\n   answerable there and is not answerable here.\n4. **This dashboard** is the early warning. It moves within a scrape interval,\n   which the other three do not.\n\nThe one panel to watch for correctness is **Usage events dropped**. Metering\nswallows its own failures so that a billing outage can never fail a\nconversation, which also means a broken meter and a quiet week look identical\neverywhere except that counter.\n\nSee `docs/guides/operate/dashboards.md` in the Fountain repo.\n"
      }
    }
